{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112181","id":2961416562,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6wg6Fy","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112181","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112181.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112181.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112181","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112181/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112181/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112181/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/7f5797833b102fc378407fc7e95d724c1bef24f6","number":112181,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add global way of accessing Delta time and Unscaled Delta time","user":{"login":"Cautami","id":219921783,"node_id":"U_kgDODRu9dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219921783?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami","html_url":"https://github.com/Cautami","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cautami/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- This PR aims to close https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7775\r\nWhich seems to be pretty positively received and additionally seems to have a general consensus that both deltas and unscaled variants should be added to the Engine class\r\n\r\nAs such, I've added the following methods:\r\n```\r\nEngine.get_delta_time()\r\nEngine.get_unscaled_delta_time()\r\nEngine.get_physics_delta_time()\r\nEngine.get_unscaled_physics_delta_time()\r\n```\r\n`get_delta` provides the exact same information the `_process` method provides. \r\n`get_physics_delta` is the same way but for `_physicsProcess`\r\n\r\nThe unscaled methods provide the user a unscaled version of both of these deltas, as they are *never* multiplied by timescale in the first place, this is the most accurate and convenient way of getting unscaled deltas. \r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\nThis is a similar to #86766, just with the extra granularity, and I guess also slightly opinionated, it seemed like the consensus on the proposal was to refer to them as Deltas, makes sense to me and matches what the average user would expect I think. \r\n\r\n[Screencast_20251029_210032.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c9f300e1-c96e-43e4-bdf4-67155d3bdc1b)\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":955079684,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NTUwNzk2ODQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/breaks%20compat","name":"breaks compat","description":"","color":"b64245","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milest